cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Seebeck Prime in your research, please cite it using these metadata or the accompanying SoftwareX article."
title: "Seebeck Prime"
subtitle: "Open-source analysis platform for experimental thermoelectric transport properties"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mostafa-kadi/Seebeck-prime"
url: "https://github.com/mostafa-kadi/Seebeck-prime"
authors:
  - family-names: Elkady
    given-names: "Mostafa M."
    # TODO(author): confirm the author list (names, ORCIDs, affiliations)
    # before the public release / Zenodo DOI minting; this entry mirrors the
    # identity declared in src/seebeck_prime/__init__.py (__author__).
keywords:
  - thermoelectrics
  - "figure of merit"
  - "Seebeck coefficient"
  - "electrical conductivity"
  - "thermal conductivity"
  - "power factor"
  - "single parabolic band model"
  - "uncertainty propagation"
abstract: >-
  Seebeck Prime is an open-source desktop application and headless Python API
  for experimental thermoelectric materials research. It processes measured
  transport data (Seebeck coefficient, electrical conductivity, total thermal
  conductivity), performs unit conversion through one unit-normalised path,
  calculates derived properties (power factor, electronic and lattice thermal
  conductivity, figure of merit, device efficiencies), propagates analytical
  uncertainties, and fits single-parabolic-band, Hall and weighted-mobility
  models, with publication-grade plotting.
